<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <parent>
    <groupId>tech.mikhailov.ratchet</groupId>
    <artifactId>ratchet-parent</artifactId>
    <version>0.21.0</version>
  </parent>
  <artifactId>ratchet-llm</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>
  <name>ratchet-llm</name>
  <description>The model wiring: the streaming reply, the thinking budget, the tool loop and the
    listener that records the wire. The JDK only.</description>
  <!-- ONE DEPENDENCY, AND IT IS THE OTHER HALF OF THIS PROJECT. Everything this module needs to
       speak to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint is in java.net.http and java.util: the request is
       written with ratchet's own Json, the response is read off the SSE frames, and the tool loop
       is fifteen lines.

       IT USED TO TAKE THREE ARTIFACTS AND THIRTEEN JARS. What that bought was one POST and one SSE
       reader; what it cost was eight megabytes reaching every consumer who wanted the retry
       schedule, an NLP toolkit and a BPE tokenizer among them, neither of which anything here has
       ever called. It also cost behaviour: three classes in this package existed to work around the
       client, and the reasoning this endpoint produces was dropped on the floor for eighty-four
       calls because it names the field `reasoning` and the client read `reasoning_content`. -->
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>tech.mikhailov.ratchet</groupId>
      <artifactId>ratchet-core</artifactId>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
</project>
